meta {
  name: 9 Gateway
  type: http
  seq: 9
}
get {
  url: {{gatewayUrl}}/health
  auth: none
}
tests {
  test("200 and Healthy", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
    expect(res.getBody()).to.match(/Healthy/i);
  });
}
docs {
  The Gateway is the eighth AppHost resource (F-015) and calls `AddServiceDefaults()` like every other
  service, so it gets the same `/health` (readiness) and `/alive` (liveness) pair. This checks the
  Gateway process itself — not the destinations it proxies to. `WaitFor` on all seven services means the
  Gateway only reports `Healthy` once every destination it could route to is also healthy.

  Every other request in this collection (everything outside `7-Health`) now goes through
  `{{gatewayUrl}}` rather than a per-service URL. The seven `*Url` variables still exist only because
  `/health` and `/alive` are not in the Gateway's `api/v1/{service}/**` allowlist — routes it doesn't
  carry, by design (T-302), so each service's own health still has to be checked directly.
}
